{"id": "EUVD-2026-103693", "enisaUuid": "df9f241f-0a96-3f7a-810b-bbc9fca2cdbe", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: close handle after create-context parsing failure\n\nSMB2_open() accounts a successful CREATE response as a remote open before\nparsing its create contexts.  If smb2_parse_contexts() rejects malformed\ncontext data, SMB2_open() returns without closing the handle, leaving the\nserver-side handle open and num_remote_opens elevated.\n\nClose the handle after a post-CREATE context parsing failure so the error\npath releases the remote resource and balances the open count.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:15:03", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eaa97a196a107d4ef8775df2248181624151812e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/80c67cc71d32ccafc89a29b669243b40d81b930f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f09875ff901e933e7b22c913daf51d21e9d93a45", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cdb36b09fb1f86d638d0afb44d621ed3f7c1d8eb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/566820af017e81497fb5e9d3ad6e7ffe2828bc8b"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98453", "GHSA-8g43-4633-h8mf"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0dca1ab8-40d8-30b0-b06a-54e15b790781", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.4.277 <5.5"}, {"id": "10c24d10-a8ba-32af-b1b7-d456c13b5440", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.7"}, {"id": "10c777b3-87d3-3eb1-921b-0d1d3b3d75e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "17621bdc-11f4-3bf6-b89c-34d996f99cb7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.150 <5.16"}, {"id": "1a568bf0-1b21-3dc4-8412-50efcdd99f03", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "13fb0fc4917621f3dfa285a27eaf7151d770b5e5"}, {"id": "1e7